@startuml
title Migration Postponement Request - Sequence Diagram

actor User

participant "Service Desk" as SD
participant "Migration Management API" as API
database "Migration Database" as DB
participant "Support Team" as Support
participant "Notification Service" as Notify

User -> SD: Create postponement request\nwith reason

SD -> API: POST /api/v1/postponement-requests

API -> DB: Validate workplace\nand active schedule
DB --> API: Workplace + schedule data

alt Workplace not found
    API --> SD: 404 WORKPLACE_NOT_FOUND

else Active postponement request already exists
    API --> SD: 409 ACTIVE_POSTPONEMENT_REQUEST_EXISTS

else Request accepted
    API -> DB: Create postponement request\nstatus = pending
    DB --> API: requestId

    API --> SD: 201 Created\npostponement request

    Support -> API: GET postponement request
    API -> DB: Read request
    DB --> API: Request data
    API --> Support: Pending request

    alt Postponement approved
        Support -> API: PATCH /postponement-requests/{requestId}\napprovalStatus = approved\nnewMigrationDate = ...

        API -> DB: Update postponement request
        API -> DB: Mark old schedule as postponed
        API -> DB: Create / update new migration schedule
        DB --> API: Updated data

        API -> Notify: Send new migration date
        Notify --> User: Migration postponed\nNew date assigned

        API --> Support: 200 OK

    else Postponement rejected
        Support -> API: PATCH /postponement-requests/{requestId}\napprovalStatus = rejected

        API -> DB: Update request\nstatus = rejected
        DB --> API: Updated request

        API -> Notify: Notify that original date remains active
        Notify --> User: Migration date unchanged

        API --> Support: 200 OK
    end
end

@enduml